#: site/templates/home.html:3
msgid "Does audio or text ever leave my Mac?"
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:3
msgid ""
"Audio never does. By default transcription and the AI model both run "
"locally, and the only network requests are the one-time model download "
"and signed update checks. If you choose to add a Claude or OpenAI key in "
"Settings, meeting text goes directly to that provider and nowhere else."
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:4
msgid "Does a bot join my call?"
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:4
msgid ""
"No. MeetMouse listens to your Mac's audio, so there is no extra "
"participant, no recording notice, and nothing for the other side to see."
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:5
msgid "What languages does it work with?"
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:5
msgid ""
"Transcription and notes work in 25 languages, including Portuguese, "
"Spanish, French, German, Japanese, and Mandarin, plus mixed-language "
"calls. The coaching cues and app menus are English for now."
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:6
msgid "Can I use it with Zoom, Meet, and Teams?"
msgstr ""

#: site/templates/home.html:6
msgid ""
"Yes. It captures the sound coming through your Mac, so it works with any "
"meeting app, browser-based calls, and even phone calls routed through "
"your Mac."
msgstr ""

