#: site/articles/blog__do-ai-notetakers-record-your-calls.html:54
msgid "The on-device exception"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__do-ai-notetakers-record-your-calls.html:55
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<a href=\"/\">MeetMouse</a> takes a different structural position: there "
"is no server side. Speech-to-text runs on your Mac (Parakeet, on-device),"
" the AI that writes the summary and coaches you is a local model pinned "
"to 127.0.0.1, and your notes stay on your Mac. No bot, no account, no "
"telemetry — the app fully works with WiFi off. It's free for 3 meetings a"
" week ({price} once for unlimited), and it writes notes and coaches you "
"live, but it's personal: if you need a shareable team archive, pair a "
"cloud tool with the guidance in the <a href=\"/blog/private-ai-meeting-"
"notes\">private meeting notes guide</a>."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:4
msgid "Fathom Pricing (2026): Free Plan Limits, Premium and Team Costs"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:5
msgid ""
"Fathom pricing explained: what the free plan includes, Premium at $20, "
"Team at $19 a seat with a 2-seat minimum, Business at $34, and what a "
"team actually pays."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:6
msgid "Fathom pricing in 2026: what the free plan gets you, and what teams pay"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:7
msgid ""
"Full disclosure: I make <a href=\"/\">MeetMouse</a>, which competes with "
"Fathom. I also think Fathom's free plan is the best free notetaker out "
"there, and I say that on every page. Here's exactly what it costs, read "
"off fathom.ai on October 20, 2026."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:9
msgid ""
"<strong>Fathom is free for individuals</strong>: unlimited recordings and"
" transcripts, instant AI summaries, clips and search. <strong>Premium is "
"$20 a month</strong> ($16 billed annually) and adds advanced summaries, "
"AI action items, Ask Fathom and a custom bot. <strong>Team is $19 per "
"user per month</strong> ($15 annually) with a 2-seat minimum, "
"<strong>Business is $34</strong> ($25 annually) and adds CRM sync and "
"scorecards, and Enterprise is a sales call. A 10-person team on Team pays"
" about $190 a month."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:11
msgid ""
"Most people searching Fathom's pricing are asking one of two questions: "
"is the free plan actually free, or what will this cost my team. Both have"
" clean answers."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:14
#: site/articles/compare__fathom-vs-fireflies.html:14
#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-fathom.html:13
msgid "Is Fathom really free?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:14
msgid ""
"Yes, for individuals. The free plan records and transcribes unlimited "
"calls and gives you instant AI summaries, clips and search across calls. "
"Advanced summaries, AI action items and Ask Fathom are on Premium at $20 "
"a month."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:15
msgid "How much does Fathom cost for a team?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:15
msgid ""
"Team is $19 per user per month billed monthly, or $15 billed annually, "
"with a 2-seat minimum. Business, which adds CRM field sync, Deal View and"
" AI scorecards, is $34 per user monthly or $25 annually. Ten people on "
"Team cost about $190 a month; on Business about $340."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:16
msgid "Does Fathom have a bot-free option?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:16
msgid ""
"Fathom's pricing page lists a choice of bot-free capture (in beta) or bot"
" capture on the free plan. By default a Fathom bot joins the call. Check "
"the current state of the beta before you count on it."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:17
msgid "What's cheaper than Fathom?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/blog__fathom-pricing.html:17
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For one person, nothing beats free. For a team, the per-seat bill is what"
" grows. MeetMouse is per person, free for 3 meetings a week, and {price} "
"once for unlimited, but it has no team workspace or CRM sync. It keeps "
"meetings on your Mac instead of in a cloud."
