"runs 100% on your Mac, coaches the <em>substance</em> of the conversation"
" against a rubric you control, and is free for 3 meetings a week or "
"{price} once for unlimited. Pick based on what you're trying to fix — and"
" where you're willing to let your meetings go."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:13
msgid "What's the difference between Poised and MeetMouse?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:13
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Both coach you live during meetings. Poised coaches delivery — filler "
"words, pace, energy — as a cloud subscription. MeetMouse coaches the "
"substance of the conversation (asks, commitments, talk balance) against a"
" rubric you control, runs 100% on your Mac, and is free for 3 meetings a "
"week or {price} once for unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:14
msgid "Does Poised work offline?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:14
msgid ""
"No — Poised processes your audio through its cloud, so it needs a "
"connection. MeetMouse runs entirely on-device and works with WiFi off."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:15
msgid "Can you customize Poised's coaching?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:15
msgid ""
"No — Poised coaches from its own model. MeetMouse's rubrics are fully "
"editable per meeting type, so you decide what it watches for."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:16
msgid "Is there a one-time-purchase alternative to Poised?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"MeetMouse is free for 3 meetings a week, or {price} once for unlimited, "
"with no account and no subscription — the only live meeting coach that "
"runs fully on-device."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:25
msgid ""
"<strong>Poised</strong> is an AI communication coach for your calls on "
"Zoom, Meet, Teams and the rest. It gives real-time feedback on how you're"
" speaking — filler words, pacing, hedging, confidence — plus post-meeting"
" reports and trend lines so you can watch yourself improve over weeks. "
"It's polished, it's established, and reviewers consistently say the "
"feedback helps."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:26
msgid ""
"<strong>MeetMouse</strong> coaches a different layer: not how you sound, "
"but what's happening in the conversation. It applies a coaching rubric to"
" the live discussion and cues you on substance — you've been monologuing "
"for two minutes, that was a range not a commitment, sounds like agreement"
" so close it out. Rubrics are yours to customize: sales calls, 1:1s, "
"interviews, fundraising. And the whole thing — transcription and AI — "
"runs on your Mac. No account, no cloud, works with WiFi off."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:36
