msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:50
msgid "Where Poised wins"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:52
msgid ""
"<strong>Delivery coaching.</strong> If your problem is \"um,\" talking "
"too fast, or sounding unsure, Poised has spent years tuning exactly that,"
" and it's good at it."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:53
msgid ""
"<strong>Long-term trend lines.</strong> Watching your filler-word count "
"drop over a month is genuinely motivating. MeetMouse keeps everything "
"local, so there's no cloud progress graph."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:54
msgid "<strong>Windows support.</strong> MeetMouse is Mac-only."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:63
msgid ""
"<strong>It coaches the meeting, not the voice.</strong> You can deliver a"
" flawless, filler-free monologue and still lose the deal because you "
"never made the ask. MeetMouse watches for the stuff that decides "
"outcomes: talk balance, vague commitments, unclosed agreements, questions"
" you didn't ask."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:64
msgid ""
"<strong>Your rubric, your rules.</strong> A sales close, a performance "
"review, and an investor pitch shouldn't be coached the same way. "
"MeetMouse's rubrics are editable — you decide what it watches for."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:65
msgid ""
"<strong>Nothing leaves your Mac. Nothing.</strong> Poised processes your "
"speech in the cloud, with an account attached. MeetMouse has no server "
"side at all — turn WiFi off and it keeps coaching. If your meetings are "
"confidential, this is the whole decision."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:66
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<strong>Free to start, then {price} once vs a subscription "
"forever.</strong> A year of any subscription coach costs more than "
"MeetMouse costs for life."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:74
msgid ""
"If public-speaking mechanics are your bottleneck — filler words, pace, "
"nerves — Poised is a fine choice and their free trial lets you test that "
"cheaply."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__meetmouse-vs-poised.html:75
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If your meetings sound fine but keep <em>ending wrong</em> — no decision,"
" no commitment, you talked the whole time — that's a substance problem, "
"and it's the one I built <a href=\"/\">MeetMouse</a> to fix. It never "
"phones home, it's free for 3 meetings a week, and if it earns its keep, "
"unlimited is {price} once."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:4
msgid "Otter vs Fathom (2026): Which AI Notetaker Should You Actually Use?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:5
msgid ""
"Otter's searchable archive vs Fathom's genuinely free notetaker — an "
"honest head-to-head from a third-party founder, plus the option neither "
"of them covers."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:6
msgid "Otter vs Fathom: which AI notetaker should you actually use?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For most individuals, <strong>Fathom wins</strong> — its free plan has no"
" minute cap, while Otter's stops at 300 minutes a month. Choose "
"<strong>Otter</strong> if cross-meeting transcript search is your daily "
"workflow and you'll pay {otter_price}/month for it. Both send a visible "
"bot by default (Fathom lists bot-free capture as a beta) and store your "
"calls in their cloud — if either of those bothers you, see the third "
"option below."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:13
msgid "Is Fathom better than Otter?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:13
msgid ""
"For most individuals, yes — Fathom's free plan has unlimited recordings "
"while Otter's caps at 300 minutes a month. Otter is better when deep "
"search across months of transcripts is your daily workflow."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:14
msgid "Do Otter and Fathom both join meetings as bots?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:14
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"By default, yes. Both join as a visible participant (Otter's desktop app "
"can record without a bot, and Fathom lists bot-free capture as a beta) "
"and record to their own cloud. If you want notes without a bot, Granola "
"does that; if you want nothing uploaded at all, MeetMouse runs 100% on-"
"device."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:15
msgid "Is Otter or Fathom cheaper?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:15
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Fathom, decisively: its individual plan is free with no minute cap. Otter"
" Pro is {otter_price}/month ({annual_cost}/year). Fathom's paid team "
"plans start at {team_price}/user/month, comparable to Otter Business."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:16
msgid "What's an alternative to both Otter and Fathom?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Granola for bot-free notes, or MeetMouse if the goal is improving your "
"meetings rather than archiving them — it coaches live, on-device, free "
"for 3 meetings a week or {price} one time for unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:25
msgid ""
"<strong>Otter</strong> is the veteran: OtterPilot joins your Zoom, Teams,"
" or Meet call, transcribes in real time, and files everything into a "
"searchable cloud workspace. The archive is the product — months later you"
" can search \"pricing discussion with Acme\" and land on the sentence."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:26
msgid ""
"<strong>Fathom</strong> is the newer favorite: same bot-joins-and-records"
" model, but the free plan is genuinely generous — unlimited recordings "
"and AI summaries for individuals — and the summaries are cleaner out of "
"the box."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:39
msgid "Where meetings live"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:39
#: site/content/alternatives.py:1
msgid "Their cloud"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:40
msgid "Killer feature"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:40
msgid "Search across months of transcripts"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:40
msgid "Free that's actually free"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:51
msgid ""
"<strong>The archive.</strong> Cross-meeting search is deeper and the "
"workspace is built for going back months. Researchers, journalists, and "
"PMs who live in old calls pick Otter."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:52
msgid ""
"<strong>Mobile.</strong> Real iOS/Android apps for in-person recording; "
"Fathom is desktop-first."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<strong>Price.</strong> The free plan covers what most individuals need "
"forever. Otter free ({free_limit}) is roughly a week of real meetings, "
"then {otter_annual}/year."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:61
msgid "300 min/month"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:62
msgid ""
"<strong>Summaries.</strong> Cleaner action-item and summary output with "
"less fiddling."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fathom.html:70
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Both put a named bot in your meeting — and some conversations visibly "
"change when it appears. Both store every word in their cloud. And both "
"are rear-view mirrors: perfect documentation of the meeting you already "
"had. If what you want is meeting notes, take Fathom (or Otter if search "
"is your job). If the bot, the cloud, or the rear-view-mirror part is your"
" actual complaint, that's a different product category: <a "
"href=\"/\">MeetMouse</a> runs 100% on your Mac, sends no bot, stores "
"nothing in any cloud, and coaches you <em>during</em> the call. Free for "
"3 meetings a week, or {price} once for unlimited. Full comparisons: <a "
"href=\"/compare/meetmouse-vs-otter\">vs Otter</a> · <a href=\"/compare"
"/meetmouse-vs-fathom\">vs Fathom</a>."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:4
msgid "Fireflies vs Otter (2026): Prices, Free Limits and Who Wins"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:5
msgid ""
"Fireflies vs Otter compared on price, free plan limits, CRM sync, search "
"and bots. Otter wins for one person, Fireflies for sales teams. Prices "
"checked October 2026."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:6
msgid "Fireflies vs Otter: which one should you pick?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:7
msgid ""
"Full disclosure: I make <a href=\"/\">MeetMouse</a>, which competes with "
"both of these sideways. It writes your notes on your Mac and coaches you "
"during the call. I don't win by trashing either one, so this is the "
"comparison I'd want if I were picking between them."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<strong>Otter</strong> is better for one person or a small team that "
"mainly wants transcripts and search: Pro is {otter_price} a month, or "
"{otter_annual_mo} billed annually. <strong>Fireflies</strong> is better "
"for sales teams that want calls pushed into the CRM, scored, and reviewed"
" by managers: Pro is {fireflies_price} a seat, Business {fireflies_biz}, "
"less on annual billing. On free plans, Otter gives you 300 minutes a "
"month but cuts each conversation at 30 minutes; Fireflies transcribes "
"without a minute cap but keeps only 400 minutes of storage per team. Both"
" send a bot into the call by default; Otter's desktop app can also record"
" without one."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:11
msgid ""
"People search \"Fireflies vs Otter\" because the two look identical from "
"the outside: a bot joins your Zoom, a transcript shows up afterwards, "
"there's an AI chat on top. The difference is who they're built for. Otter"
" is a memory for you. Fireflies is a system for your sales manager."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:14
msgid "Is Fireflies or Otter better?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:14
msgid ""
"Otter, if you're one person or a small team who mainly needs transcripts "
"and search. Fireflies, if you run a sales team and want calls synced to "
"the CRM, scored and reviewed by managers. If you just want free notes, "
"Fathom's free plan beats both."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:15
msgid "Is Fireflies more expensive than Otter?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:15
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Slightly, per seat. Billed monthly, Otter Pro is {otter_price} and "
"Fireflies Pro is {fireflies_price} a seat. On annual billing it's "
"{otter_annual_mo} vs {fireflies_annual_mo}. At the team tier, Otter "
"Business is {otter_biz} a user monthly and Fireflies Business is "
"{fireflies_biz} a seat. Prices from otter.ai and fireflies.ai on October "
"20, 2026."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:16
msgid "Which has the better free plan, Otter or Fireflies?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:16
msgid ""
"Depends on your meetings. Otter's free plan gives you 300 minutes a "
"month, stops each conversation at 30 minutes and keeps your 25 most "
"recent. Fireflies' free plan transcribes without a minute cap but has "
"limited AI summaries and only 400 minutes of storage per team. For long "
"meetings, neither free plan holds up."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:17
msgid "Do Otter and Fireflies join my meeting as a bot?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:17
msgid ""
"By default, yes. Both join as a visible participant (Otter's desktop app "
"can record without a bot) and store recordings and transcripts in their "
"cloud. Fireflies also pushes them into your CRM. Bot-free options: "
"Granola (cloud notes, no bot) or MeetMouse (no bot, on your Mac)."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:18
msgid "What's a private alternative to Otter and Fireflies?"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:18
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"MeetMouse. Transcription and its default AI run on your Mac, no bot "
"joins, and nothing is uploaded. You get a summary and next steps plus "
"live coaching during the call, but no cloud archive or CRM sync. Free for"
" 3 meetings a week, or {price} once for unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:26
msgid "What each tool actually is"
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:27
msgid ""
"<strong>Otter</strong> records and transcribes your meetings through its "
"bot, then files everything into a searchable workspace. It's been doing "
"this longer than almost anyone, and search across months of conversations"
" is the thing it does best. Think of it as a memory: for you first, and "
"for your team if you share."
msgstr ""

#: site/articles/compare__otter-vs-fireflies.html:28
msgid ""
"<strong>Fireflies</strong> records the same way, then goes corporate. "
"Transcripts flow into CRM records, calls get scored, managers get "
"dashboards of talk time and topics across every rep. Think of it as "
"infrastructure for a revenue team. The individual rep is not really the "
"customer; the person running the team is."
msgstr ""

