#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker name suggestions now appear right beside the talk bubble with Yes"
" and No buttons, so you can confirm a name during the call without "
"opening MeetMouse."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker snapshots no longer misread a capital I as a lowercase L in names"
" (for example, \"lvan\" instead of \"Ivan\")."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker snapshots recognize the standalone Google Meet app. The window "
"chooser shows detected calls first, with an option to select the call you"
" switch to."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker snapshots can read Google Meet’s blue speaker outlines as well as"
" Zoom’s green/yellow outlines. Participant names must be visible; matches"
" still need your confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker-name settings now explain Zoom’s name-visibility option. When all"
" snapshots miss the names, MeetMouse explains how to name a speaker "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Calls now run lighter by default. New installs start with advanced live "
"coaching off, so no large AI model downloads or runs during calls, and "
"built-in nudges still work. A setup checklist on the home screen offers "
"your Claude account or a local model for AI notes after each call. Want "
"AI nudges during calls? Turn on advanced live coaching in Settings → AI, "
"which now shows what it costs in memory on your Mac. Existing installs "
"keep their current setting."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"When a call plays through your Mac's built-in speakers, MeetMouse now "
"shows a one-line tip to use headphones. Without them your mic also hears "
"the other side, so their words can show up as yours or both sides can "
"blend into one block. Dismiss it with the x for that meeting."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Press Control–Command–M from any app to open MeetMouse while it’s running"
" in the menu bar. Disable the shortcut in Settings → General."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Right after a meeting's notes are ready, MeetMouse offers once to copy a "
"private link to send them to the people in the meeting. Dismiss it and it"
" won't ask for that meeting; dismiss it three meetings in a row and it "
"stops asking."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Shared notes pages now credit MeetMouse with a small link to the site."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Invite links now send friends straight to the free download."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"When your free week of unlimited meetings ends, MeetMouse tells you once "
"(3 free meetings a week from here, notes never locked) instead of waiting"
" until a meeting won't start."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetMouse is now free. New installs get unlimited meetings for the first "
"week, then 3 meetings a week (resets Monday). Your notes, transcripts and"
" search are never locked. For unlimited meetings, invite 2 friends with "
"your link (Get MeetMouse Unlimited, in the menu bar or sidebar), pay $20 "
"once, or enter an AppSumo code. Everyone who installed MeetMouse before "
"this version keeps unlimited automatically."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed meetings not stopping automatically after a Zoom call. Zoom 7 (Zoom"
" Workplace) renamed its windows' owner, so MeetMouse never saw the "
"meeting window and could not tell the call had ended; the meeting window "
"is now recognized by the app's identity instead of its display name. "
"Automatic speaker snapshots find the Zoom 7 window again for the same "
"reason."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Shared meeting notes now live at meetmouse.com links. Links created "
"earlier on rhinovoice.app keep working."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If the other side of a call goes silent because macOS stopped delivering "
"system audio — a headset connecting mid-call, a display sleeping, or a "
"locked screen — MeetMouse now rebuilds the capture automatically and "
"keeps trying until it returns. Before, the rest of the call could be "
"missing the other person with \"Listening (you + them)\" still showing."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker snapshots can now name the other person on one-on-one Zoom calls "
"with no speaker highlight, such as while they share their screen. Add "
"your name under Settings → General → Speaker names so MeetMouse can tell "
"your tile from theirs. The name still needs your confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Optional automatic speaker snapshots: enable once to detect your meeting "
"window and suggest speaker names each meeting. Images stay on-device and "
"are discarded; names still need confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker snapshots now explain when no visible names were read and that "
"suggestions require a reliable voice match, instead of implying that "
"suggestions are ready."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetMouse now warns you when it can't hear your microphone — for example "
"when microphone access is off or your Mac's selected mic is silent (a "
"MacBook's built-in mic is off with the lid closed). Before, your side of "
"the meeting could go missing from the transcript with no sign anything "
"was wrong."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Optional speaker snapshots: automatically detect your meeting window to "
"help match visible speaker names to voices. Up to six snapshots are read "
"on-device and discarded; suggested names need your confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed an echo-filter issue that could remove your replies when they "
"reused words from the other speaker’s question, including French coaching"
" conversations."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Multi-language meetings: choose \"Auto-detect\" to transcribe any of the "
"25 supported languages, even several in one call. Change the language in "
"one click under Start meeting, from the Meeting Detected pill, or mid-"
"meeting from the meeting header; your recent languages stay at the top. "
"AI notes can follow the meeting's language or always be written in "
"English."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The talk bubble now defaults to a slim, rounded vertical shape on the "
"right edge of your screen. Choose Floating or Right edge and Horizontal "
"or Vertical in General settings; your saved choices are preserved."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"AI notes now generate automatically after meetings even when live AI "
"coaching is off or could not load. If AI is unavailable, a basic recap "
"remains available."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Ending a meeting now always opens its notes. Previously only the first "
"meeting after launching the app did; later ones went back to the home "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Double-click the meeting bubble to open MeetMouse."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Removed the extra stop button from the top of the live meeting view. End "
"a meeting from the Stop button in the sidebar or the menu bar."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Delete saved meetings from their detail view, with confirmation and "
"cleanup of the local transcript, notes, and chat."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meeting titles now describe the purpose, confirmed participants, and "
"company context instead of guessing names from repeated words. "
"Regenerating notes upgrades old keyword titles while preserving manual "
"renames."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The meeting bubble's activity bars move faster and more smoothly."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Local AI coaching no longer reserves transcription memory twice at "
"meeting startup, allowing smaller models to run with less available "
"memory. Model selection labels now distinguish installed models from "
"running AI."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The floating meeting overlay is now a compact bubble with a timer, "
"speaker-colored activity bars, and vertical talk-share edges. Coaching "
"nudges and warnings still expand when needed."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Connect your Claude subscription in Settings → AI to power coaching, "
"meeting reviews and chat through Claude Code, with no API key required. "
"Text sharing remains opt-in; audio stays on your Mac."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Finished meetings open directly to Notes, including when you reopen the "
"window after a call."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Share notes now generates missing AI notes automatically, then creates "
"and copies the private link with visible progress and retryable errors, "
"without an extra confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Share notes is one click now: it creates and copies the private link "
"right away and opens the ready-to-send screen, with no preview "
"confirmation in between"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The AI provider control in the bottom-left of the sidebar is now a "
"compact gear icon; hover it for the label"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meetings are now the home screen. A cleaner meetings list replaces the "
"coaching dashboard as the starting view; coaching progress stays one "
"click away in the sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Open a saved meeting and it lands in a dedicated AI chat: suggested "
"questions, follow-ups, copyable answers, and a stop button. Chats save "
"locally and restore when you return, and clicking an answer's timestamp "
"jumps to that spot in the transcript. Notes, transcript, and coaching "
"stay one click away"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Share meeting notes with an encrypted, expiring web link: click Share "
"notes on any saved meeting. Only your curated notes and next steps go out"
" — never the transcript, coaching, or chats — encrypted on your Mac "
"before upload, and links expire after 30 days. Preview first, then copy "
"or send; stop sharing anytime from the meeting or from Meetings → Shared "
"links"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Recipients open shared notes without an account, can forward the link or "
"copy the next steps, and see a small MeetMouse mention after the content"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Optional cloud AI: add a Claude or OpenAI API key in Settings → AI to run"
" coaching, reviews, and Ask AI on a cloud model. Local stays the default."
" Meeting text is shared only after you opt in, audio is never uploaded, "
"and keys live in the macOS Keychain on this device only"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Live view: larger transcript text with clearer speaker headings, a "
"coaching pane that opens by default and can be hidden, and a slimmer "
"sidebar you can hide to focus on the conversation. Scrolling back pauses "
"auto-scroll; Back to live resumes it"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meeting questions keep the topic of recent follow-ups, pull in more "
"surrounding transcript context, and cite timestamps from the local model"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Post-meeting notes now refresh as soon as AI generation finishes, and "
"watching the demo no longer blocks the Meetings and Coaching buttons"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker names now come only from the people you confirm in this call's "
"setup. MeetMouse no longer reaches back to whoever you met with last time"
" — that guest's name can't appear on live text, ASR hints, coaching "
"prompts, saved titles, filenames, or transcript metadata for a call they "
"weren't part of"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Naming one person no longer names everyone. Previously a single named "
"voice was taken as proof of a one-on-one, so unassigned speech inherited "
"that name; now a second detected voice suspends the guess and each "
"speaker keeps their own label"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Saved voice profiles are cleaner: a speaker's voice clip now excludes "
"other people's overlapping speech, so a crosstalk moment can't be learned"
" as someone's voice. If less than three seconds of solo speech is "
"available, no profile is saved rather than a bad one"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetMouse now actually shows up as \"MeetMouse\" in Finder, the Dock, and"
" Spotlight. If you updated from Meeting Coach, the app on disk kept its "
"old `MeetingCoach.app` filename — it renames itself once on the next "
"launch and reopens straight away. Settings, models, transcripts, "
"permissions, and updates all carry over untouched"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The app has a new name and face: MeetMouse, with a phone-listening gray "
"mouse on NoahKagan green throughout the app and the same recognizable "
"animal in the menu bar. Your settings, models, transcripts, and updates "
"continue exactly where they left off"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If you had connected an AI agent, re-add it: the built-in MCP server "
"moved with the rename. Open Advanced → Agent access and copy the new "
"`claude mcp add` command — an older `meetingcoach` entry points at a path"
" that no longer exists"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meeting reviews are now organized by topic: a NOTES section with a "
"heading per subject discussed and dense factual bullets under each, plus "
"NEXT STEPS with an owner on every item — instead of one flat list of "
"takeaways. Long meetings fit whole: a 43-minute call is reviewed "
"untrimmed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Reviews stick closer to what was actually said: someone who was mentioned"
" is no longer written up as if they spoke, and no deadlines are invented "
"that nobody committed to. Reviews saved by earlier versions still open as"
" before"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Search matches every word you type, in any order, and highlights each "
"match — \"pricing anna\" finds the meeting where Anna raised pricing, "
"however the words fell"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New \"Ask AI\" card in search results: ask a question across your saved "
"meetings (\"what did we decide about the launch date?\") and get an "
"answer that cites which meeting each point came from. Runs on your local "
"model; if none is installed, or no meeting matches, it says so"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Open any saved meeting and ask it questions in the new ask bar at the "
"bottom — answers come from that meeting's transcript and review only"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The AI model picker now shows each model's download size next to its name"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New \"AI coaching\" toggle in Settings → Model: turn it off and "
"MeetingCoach runs transcript-first — live transcript, speaker names, and "
"built-in nudges keep working, but no AI model is loaded. Flip it off mid-"
"call and the memory (~7 GB for the default model) comes back right away, "
"not next session. \"Generate AI review\" on saved sessions still works on"
" demand"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If the AI model is slowing your Mac, a 🐢 tip now appears in the main "
"window and floating overlay with a one-click way to turn AI coaching off;"
" the low-memory banner offers the same. Decline it three times and it "
"stays quiet"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Transcripts now live in `~/Documents/MeetingCoach/transcripts/`, named by"
" date and title (e.g. `2026-08-31T14-30_partner-sync_chad-anna.md`) so a "
"file listing reads as a timeline, with a small `.json` file beside each "
"one and a running `index.jsonl` — point Claude, ChatGPT, or any AI tool "
"at that one folder and it gets transcripts and nothing else. Your "
"existing sessions are copied in (never moved or renamed) the first time "
"you launch"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed one person showing up as two speakers in a one-on-one when you had "
"saved them under two names (like \"anna\" and \"Anna Jones\"): their "
"turns no longer flip between names, and short replies stay attributed. If"
" two labels still look like the same person, a one-tap \"sound like the "
"same person\" card merges them — transcript, timeline, and saved voice "
"profile included"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Voice recognition now only looks for the people who are actually on the "
"call (the guests you listed in pre-call setup, or your 4 most recent "
"contacts) instead of everyone you've ever named"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The Coach suggestions card now says what clicking does — \"Space it out\""
" shows the real wait it proposes (\"about 90s between repeats instead of "
"60s\"), \"Turn it off\" / \"Keep it\" replace the vague Apply/Dismiss — "
"and it no longer proposes spacing out a nudge that is already at its "
"limit"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed a fresh install occasionally running without AI coaching: if the "
"first transcription-model download failed and you clicked Retry, the AI "
"model download that was supposed to follow never started until the next "
"launch"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Picking a different AI model during a live session now says what actually"
" happens: the session keeps the model it started with, and your new pick "
"takes over from your next session — before, the change looked ignored"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The low-memory banner now tells you when a small model is installed and "
"ready for your next session, instead of going quiet right after its "
"download finishes"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"When the full AI coach cannot load because your Mac is busy or low on "
"memory, the main window and floating overlay now say “Basic mode” instead"
" of leaving you wondering why no AI nudges appear; built-in coaching "
"keeps working"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetingCoach now tries smaller AI models you already downloaded before "
"falling back to basic mode"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If you do not have a lightweight fallback yet, the low-memory banner "
"offers a one-click ~2.1 GB download for future meetings without changing "
"your preferred model"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed named speakers occasionally losing their name on short replies in a"
" one-on-one call when speaker detection briefly imagined an extra voice "
"that never said anything"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash that could quit MeetingCoach as a meeting started, when a "
"headset or other microphone was still connecting. The app now gives the "
"mic a moment to settle, and if it never becomes usable it says so instead"
" of quitting"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetingCoach now speaks your language: meetings can be transcribed in 25 "
"languages — English plus 24 European languages, from Spanish and French "
"to Ukrainian and Greek. Pick yours in Settings → General; by default it "
"follows your Mac's language"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Non-English meetings use a new high-accuracy on-device engine (Apple "
"Silicon, one ~600 MB download the first time). Your audio still never "
"leaves your Mac"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Post-meeting notes and reviews are written in the meeting's language, and"
" saved sessions remember their language — regenerating an old review "
"keeps it"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"In non-English meetings, live coaching sticks to what works in any "
"language: talk time, voice share, and running over time. English meetings"
" keep the full set"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The language you pick is locked in when a meeting starts, so changing it "
"mid-call never scrambles a running transcript. Intel Macs stay English-"
"only (explained right in Settings)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetMouse now checks how much memory is actually free once a call is "
"underway — not just how much your Mac has — and picks a lighter model "
"when your machine is busy. A 32 GB Mac with a lot already open no longer "
"slows to a crawl mid-meeting"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If nothing can run safely, coaching continues without the AI parts "
"instead of freezing your call, and it stays that way for the whole "
"meeting rather than loading a model at the end"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"A meeting now uses exactly one model from start to finish, and always "
"releases it when the call is over — including when you stop before saying"
" anything"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Models are no longer loaded speculatively when a meeting is detected: "
"your Mac only holds one while a call is actually running"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Naming speakers is now dependable: rename someone once and they stay "
"named — including the words they said before the transcript learned to "
"tell voices apart, and anything they say next. On a two-person call, "
"naming the other person (or listing them in pre-call setup) labels the "
"whole far side with their name; if a third voice joins, the transcript "
"honestly goes back to numbered speakers"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Naming someone in the first moments of a call now still saves their voice"
" — the app waits for enough speech and saves automatically, then keeps "
"the fullest sample at the end of the call so future meetings recognize "
"them"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Renaming a speaker after a session ends now updates the saved transcript "
"too, so the name is still there when you reopen it"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The rename popover suggests people you've already named or met with — "
"start typing and pick, or click a suggestion straight away"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Speaker names now show a pencil icon on hover and a one-time hint on your"
" first real meeting, so it's obvious they're editable"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Updates now install themselves: they download quietly in the background "
"and apply the next time the app isn't running — never during a meeting. "
"No more missing a fix because an update popup got dismissed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If an update has been waiting a few days (this app rarely quits, so it "
"rarely gets the chance to install), the app offers it right after a call "
"ends — at most once a day, and never while you're in one. The menu bar "
"shows how long it's been waiting"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Prefer to review each update yourself? Settings → General → \"Install "
"updates automatically\" turns the automatic behavior off; the menu bar "
"dot still tells you when one is ready"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The app now records its version when it starts, so support questions get "
"answered from your first log line instead of guesswork"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"A red dot on the menu bar icon shows when an update is waiting, with "
"\"Update available…\" pinned to the top of the dropdown — so a dismissed "
"update popup doesn't mean a missed update"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on Intel Macs: the high-accuracy transcription model only "
"runs on Apple Silicon, and starting a session on an Intel Mac could quit "
"the app mid-meeting. Intel Macs now automatically use Apple's built-in "
"transcription instead, and the app says clearly (during setup and in each"
" session) that Intel isn't fully supported — reduced accuracy, no speaker"
" identification. Intel Macs also no longer download the unusable 600 MB "
"model"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"The truth about FaceTime and phone calls on your Mac: macOS blocks every "
"app from hearing them — including the microphone itself, which goes "
"silent for other apps the moment a call connects. Previously the app "
"pretended to listen anyway and blamed you for 100% of the talking; now it"
" detects the call and tells you straight, with what actually works: "
"answer on your iPhone on speakerphone near your Mac, or use Zoom/Meet for"
" coached calls"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The microphone also now notices when it's receiving dead silence (a call "
"grabbed it mid-session, a device glitch) and reconnects automatically "
"instead of listening to nothing forever"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"FaceTime and iPhone calls taken on your Mac are now real meetings: they "
"trigger the \"Meeting detected\" prompt just like Zoom, and call sessions"
" are titled with the caller's name"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"When a call's audio never reaches your Mac (you answered on the iPhone, "
"or it's playing in a headset), the app now says \"Can't hear this "
"meeting\" with how to fix it — instead of showing \"Listening\" over an "
"empty transcript and then blaming a quiet room"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Sessions get real names: the AI review that reads your whole meeting now "
"titles it — \"Dana · pricing & renewal\" instead of a word collage. Your "
"own renames always win"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The AI model frees its memory (several GB) whenever you're not in a "
"meeting — it loads the moment a meeting is detected and unloads after "
"your recap is ready"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Lower processor use during calls: coaching skips AI passes when the "
"conversation hasn't moved, and transcription stops re-reading long "
"monologues every second"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: quiet speech close to the mic could be silently discarded as "
"speaker echo"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Phone calls on your Mac no longer silence coaching: handing a call to the"
" Mac makes the iPhone's microphone the system input, which delivers "
"nothing to other apps — the app kept saying \"Listening\" over an empty "
"transcript. It now detects that and listens through the Mac's own "
"microphone instead, whether the call started before or during your "
"session"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Granola re-import now repairs meetings that came in empty: if an earlier "
"import left a meeting without its transcript (a bug fixed in 0.12.0), "
"importing the same export again fills the transcript in instead of saying"
" \"already imported\" — your renames and notes stay untouched"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The Questions to Ask, Coaching Notes, and Model rows in Advanced now open"
" with a click anywhere on the row, not just the tiny chevron"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: switching audio devices mid-meeting (taking a phone call on your "
"Mac, connecting AirPods, plugging in a headset) silently killed the "
"microphone — the app kept saying \"Listening\" but stopped transcribing. "
"It now detects the change and reconnects to your mic automatically"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"No more picking an AI model that's too big for your Mac: the app now "
"knows how much memory you have — the model list only shows ones that will"
" run well, the recommended download matches your machine, and the biggest"
" models stay reserved for Macs that can handle them"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"If a too-big model does end up selected (say, from before this update), "
"you get a clear orange note in Settings and the app quietly uses your "
"best-fitting installed model instead — no more whole-Mac freeze mid-"
"meeting"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The AI model now loads when the app starts, not in the first minute of "
"your call — meetings begin with coaching ready instead of your Mac "
"straining right when the call gets going"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Under the hood: removed a chunk of leftover code from retired features, "
"so the app is a little leaner"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"A fresh coat of paint everywhere: new AppSumo-yellow Go live button, "
"cleaner type, and a simpler title bar — same layout and flow you already "
"know"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Follows your Mac's appearance: light, dark, or auto — the new design now "
"has a proper dark side"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meeting reviews became real meeting notes: a headline-first summary, "
"takeaways with the actual numbers and names, and next steps as \"who — "
"what — by when\". Old sessions can be rewritten too — open one and hit "
"\"Regenerate with AI\" in the Summary tab"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: if the AI model you'd selected was never finished downloading, "
"every AI feature (reviews, name suggestions, smart nudges) silently did "
"nothing — the app now uses whichever model is actually installed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Sessions open in tabs — Transcript, Summary, Coaching — with Copy and "
"Export (Markdown, plain text, or just the summary)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The sessions list shows friendly dates instead of filenames, and \"See "
"all\" reveals your full history"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Your Progress is the home screen again, redesigned to match"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Granola import actually works now — validated against a real export: your"
" meetings come in with their true titles, notes, and full searchable "
"transcripts (the first version choked on the file format and imported "
"empty shells)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Naming a speaker sticks: tagging someone while they're still labeled "
"\"Them\" saved nothing before (you had to wait for \"Them 1\") — now "
"every tag saves their voice locally so future meetings can label them "
"automatically"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Much lower CPU during meetings: a bug ran two transcription engines at "
"once every session (Apple's engine on the other side's audio even when "
"the fast Parakeet model was loaded), and transcription re-processed audio"
" far more often than needed — both fixed, along with meeting detection "
"scanning your windows every 2 seconds mid-meeting"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Sessions are now named after the real meeting when possible — the Meet "
"tab or Zoom topic (\"Weekly Sync\") instead of a guessed \"person · "
"topic\" — and search finds chats by name, not just by what was said"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The floating overlay behaves: it stays where you drag it (forever), "
"closing it keeps it closed for the rest of the meeting, and Settings → "
"General has a switch to turn it off entirely — nudges still show in the "
"main window"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The meeting-detected pill stopped repeating itself (\"& open MeetMouse\" "
"line removed), and a start that fails no longer silences the pill for the"
" rest of that meeting"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Renaming a chat back to its date now sticks instead of a topic name "
"reappearing"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when editing lists with a row deleted mid-edit — typing in "
"a vocabulary term, pre-call participant, or custom coaching signal and "
"removing a row could quit the app and lose what you typed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Vocabulary edits now confirm themselves: a green \"Saved\" appears when a"
" term is stored, and a hint tells you when a row still needs its "
"\"Corrected to…\" filled in to save"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New first-run checklist: the main pane walks you to your first coached "
"meeting — two permissions with Grant buttons, both models downloading "
"with real progress bars (they start on their own, no clicks), then \"join"
" a meeting\""
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Coming from Granola? Export your meetings as a CSV in Granola, pick the "
"file in Settings → General, and your notes become searchable MeetMouse "
"sessions — on your Mac, like everything else"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The give-MeetMouse-to-a-friend prompt now waits for your second coached "
"meeting instead of interrupting the glow of the first"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: at narrow widths the coach panel could clip its cards on both "
"edges, cutting text mid-word — the panel now refuses to shrink past "
"readable"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The sidebar's Advanced section starts open so Questions to Ask and "
"Coaching Notes are visible, and the whole header row is clickable"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"MeetMouse now starts automatically when you log in (so it's ready after a"
" restart) — turn it off any time in Settings → General → Startup"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Coaching now stops when your meeting ends, even with a TV or podcast "
"playing nearby — background audio no longer keeps the session (and the "
"transcript) running past the call"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The other side's words now read as full sentences: transcripts save whole"
" thoughts with one timestamp each, instead of shredded 1-3 word lines"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Stray \"Siri\" / \"Hey Siri\" pickups from a phone or HomePod in the room"
" no longer land in your transcript"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Product names come out right: known garbles fix themselves (\"app sumo\" "
"→ AppSumo, \"tidy cow\" → TidyCal), and a rare bug that rendered English "
"phrases in Vietnamese characters is repaired automatically"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Click a misheard word in the transcript to fix it — the word comes pre-"
"filled, you type what it should be, and the fix applies on the spot, to "
"the rest of the call, and to every future meeting (right-click a line for"
" multi-word phrases); your term list lives in Settings → General → "
"Vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"First sessions now say when transcript accuracy is reduced: a banner "
"during the call (and a note on the review) explains the high-accuracy "
"engine is still downloading and will be ready next session — no more "
"\"why did it only catch random words?\""
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Give MeetMouse to a friend for FREE: grab an invite from the menu bar "
"(you have 3) — one click copies a ready-to-send message with a code your "
"friend redeems free on AppSumo"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"After your first coached meeting, MeetMouse asks if you know someone "
"who'd want it too"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The transcript now tells remote speakers apart: on a group call, \"Them\""
" splits into \"Them 1\", \"Them 2\", … as each person talks"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Click any speaker's label to name them — the whole transcript relabels, "
"and their voice is remembered on your Mac so future meetings greet them "
"by name from the first sentence"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The coach spots names on its own (\"Them 1 sounds like Sarah\") and "
"offers a one-click confirm — it never applies a name without you"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "People you list in the call's goal form are recognized first"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Voice matching runs entirely on-device, like everything else — no audio "
"or voice data ever leaves your Mac"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Tuned to stay light on long calls: less memory for audio, less work per "
"second"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Your Progress now counts real weeks: \"this week\" starts Monday, "
"compared against all of last week — no more rolling 7-day windows that "
"read like wrong numbers"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Coach suggestion cards now say exactly what Apply will do (\"waits 50% "
"longer between nudges\", \"starts watching for this next call\") instead "
"of leaving you guessing"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Coaching Notes now actually learn from anything you paste: feedback from "
"Claude or any AI tool gets read by your local model — known signals tune "
"up, and brand-new patterns (\"you keep selling after they've said yes\") "
"become proposed signals you approve on the Progress dashboard before the "
"coach starts watching for them"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Installed models are recognized the moment the app opens — no more "
"\"Download Model\" showing over a model you already downloaded"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Time-based nudges (\"1min left\", time check, overrun) now only run when "
"you give the call a length — set it in the goal form, or pick a default "
"for every call in Settings → General"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Questions to Ask clears itself when the call ends, ready for the next "
"meeting's list — and still ticks off automatically as you ask them, with "
"a tap to override either way"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"\"What was said\" appears only on nudges that have an actual moment to "
"quote"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The coach panel can be dragged much wider, and Progress tiles now say "
"what they measure: your last 7 days vs the prior 7"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Your post-meeting review is now about the conversation itself — the "
"summary, key takeaways, and next steps come from what was actually said, "
"decided, and promised on the call; coaching feedback lives only in \"Next"
" meeting focus\""
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The Questions to Ask checklist is clickable during the call — tick a "
"question off yourself, or untick one it marked by mistake (it stays "
"unticked)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"\"Great question\" nudges now quote the question you asked and how they "
"opened up — not a random slice from the middle of their answer"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Your post-meeting review is now a proper card — summary, key takeaways, "
"and next steps you can check off (they stay checked). Both the instant "
"review and the AI review use it, and old saved reviews render in the same"
" clean layout"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Sessions name themselves: \"Lindsay · radar & group\" instead of a date, "
"worked out from who you talked to and what about, with the date shown "
"alongside. Right-click to rename"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Click a session to read it right in the app — color-coded transcript, its"
" review up top, and one click copies the whole meeting for Slack, email, "
"or an AI tool"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New under Advanced: Questions to Ask — paste the questions you always "
"want covered and they show as a live checklist that ticks off as you ask "
"them (per-meeting questions live in the goal form)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Nudge cards can show the exact words behind a nudge (\"What was said\"), "
"say what window they're judging (\"last 5 min\"), and take thumbs up/down"
" feedback"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The floating overlay returns if you closed it mid-meeting and moves to "
"the screen your call is on; praise stays up a little longer"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Joining a Google Meet in the browser now prompts in about 10 seconds (was"
" 40) and the prompt names the platform — Meet, Hangouts, or Zoom-in-"
"browser"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Coaching Notes now save on their own — tell the coach \"watch my talk "
"time\" without pairing a transcript"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Agent access (MCP) setup moved to Settings → General"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"A calmer, simpler MeetMouse: the live transcript is now the main event, "
"with your talk-time split and elapsed time shown as quiet ambient info — "
"not warnings"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Far fewer interruptions: only a handful of high-value nudges fire by "
"default (talk time, one question at a time, action items, locking a real "
"date, one genuine win). Everything else moved to Coaching Style, off by "
"default — re-enable any signal you miss"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Zero setup to start: no goal step, no AI-nudges toggle, no focus picker. "
"Goal setup and coaching customization live under Advanced; AI nudges and "
"the meeting summary switch on automatically when a local model is "
"installed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Your recap now generates itself when you stop — summary, action items, "
"and talk split, no button"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Search your chats: one search box over every saved conversation, grouped "
"by meeting with the moment highlighted"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Connect Claude and other AI agents to your meetings: a built-in MCP "
"server lets agents list, search, and read your saved transcripts — fully "
"local, over stdio, nothing leaves your Mac. Setup: open Advanced → Agent "
"access → copy the `claude mcp add` command (or point your agent at "
"`MeetMouse.app/Contents/MacOS/meetmouse-mcp`)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Stopping a session keeps your whole transcript on screen — including the "
"words you were still saying when you hit Stop (they now land in the saved"
" session too)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Nudges and Transcript panes are back to clean white; the warm tint stays "
"in the sidebar only"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Coaching now reliably stops when your meeting ends — saying goodbye right"
" before hanging up no longer made it miss the ending"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "No more \"You're still talking\" while you wait alone for others to join"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Your saved coaching notes now actually tune the coach — pasted feedback "
"teaches the signals it names, and the save button shows what it learned"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"A calmer, lighter look: warm paper background, serif titles, quieter "
"nudge cards, and human signal names (\"Stacked Qs\", not "
"\"stackedQuestions\")"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New recommended AI model: Qwen 3.5 — sharper coaching judgment, faster on"
" Apple Silicon, and a smaller download"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Model catalog refreshed: Qwen 3.5 in three sizes and IBM Granite 4 added,"
" older models retired"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New: auto-start coaching — turn it on and coaching begins by itself when "
"a meeting is detected, after a 10-second cancelable countdown"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meeting-end detection got smarter: coaching stops within seconds of "
"leaving a Zoom, Meet, or huddle — and never cuts you off mid-sentence"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Nudges quiet down when you ignore them, in the moment and over time"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Copy the whole transcript with one click after a call"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Settings got tabs: pick where transcripts are saved, and your stats live "
"next door"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Clearer warning when the app can only hear your mic"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Faster and lighter, especially in hour-long sessions"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Everything now lives in one main window — no more separate windows to "
"juggle"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Coaching stops automatically when your meeting ends"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Slack huddles are now detected"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Dictation no longer triggers \"meeting detected\""
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Meetings in the browser (Meet, Zoom web) are detected more reliably"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New here? The progress pane now walks you through your first session in "
"three steps"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Fixed a crash when notification permission was denied"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Meetings are detected on any microphone, not just the default input"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "New: launch MeetMouse at login"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Quit straight from the menu bar dropdown"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Meeting auto-detect is now ON by default for fresh installs"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Updates arrive faster — the app checks hourly instead of daily"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The Coaching Style sheet closes itself after a successful save"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Transcript export now uses a Zoom-style format, and speaker turns split "
"cleanly at speaker boundaries"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The local AI engine restarts itself if it ever dies mid-session"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The meeting-detected card gains a hover-to-reveal close button"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "A redesigned, more polished meeting-detected card"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Send feedback straight from the menu bar dropdown"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Sessions start instantly — no more waiting on the transcription-model "
"download; the higher-accuracy engine fetches in the background and takes "
"over next session"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Coaching styles work without a local AI model via built-in presets"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Fixed wall-of-text transcripts when running mic-only"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New to MeetMouse? A short demo replays a sample meeting with real nudges "
"on first launch — no mic, no permissions, no downloads"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Live talk meter: a thin You/Them bar in the overlay and transcript shows "
"your share of the conversation as it happens (orange past 65%)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Reviews work without an AI model: an instant on-device review appears "
"after every session; the AI review remains when a model is installed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Share your recap: copy or share the post-meeting review (summary, talk "
"ratio, commitments) straight to Slack or email"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Make the coach yours: the new Coaching Style panel turns a plain-English "
"description (\"coach me to stop rambling\") into your own rubric — toggle"
" any signal, tune how eagerly it fires, add custom signals the AI watches"
" live"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The coach now improves itself, with your approval: it proposes rubric "
"changes backed by your feedback (\"you rated this Wrong 8 of 10 times — "
"turn it off?\"); nothing changes silently"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Your progress lives in the main window: day streaks, week-over-week nudge"
" and talk-share trends, top patterns, and up to two focus goals that "
"sharpen the signals you care about"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Tell it your role: coaching setup tunes the rubric to how you sell, "
"manage, or run meetings"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Meeting auto-detect (off by default): a menu bar icon offers \"Start "
"coaching?\" when a meeting app and your mic go live — recording never "
"starts without your click"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Export your transcript: after a session ends, a small download button "
"appears at the top of the transcript panel — click it to save the "
"transcript as a text file"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"The coach now praises too: green nudges reinforce your best moves the "
"moment they happen — a great open question that gets them talking, "
"handing someone the decision, refocusing a drifting room, locking "
"commitments, and reflecting their point back"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Much more accurate transcripts — a new on-device engine (Parakeet) "
"replaces Apple's speech recognizer. Still 100% on your Mac; downloads a "
"~600 MB model on first session (falls back to the old engine if the model"
" can't load)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: the other side's voice no longer bleeds into your (\"You\") side "
"of the transcript when you're on speakers — measured on a real call, "
"wrong-speaker words dropped from ~3,800 to ~500"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Their side of the transcript now comes through in full sentences instead "
"of 2-3 word fragments, and stops dropping quiet words"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: large blank spaces between transcript lines, and lines duplicating"
" once speakers were identified"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: transcripts turning into garbled fragments during calls (a 0.4.3 "
"regression)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: starting a session no longer reduces your call or system volume at"
" all"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Smoother transcripts — sentences no longer get chopped into fragments "
"during pauses"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The mic no longer switches into \"call mode\" when a session starts"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: starting a session no longer makes the rest of your Mac's audio "
"very quiet"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Transcripts now tell speakers apart — turns are labeled Speaker 1, "
"Speaker 2, … on phone and in-person calls, processed 100% on your Mac"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Words appear in the transcript as you say them, instead of arriving in "
"delayed chunks"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Fixed: transcription silently produced nothing on some microphone setups"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Fixed: high CPU usage when no audio was flowing"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Adding participant names in Pre-Call Setup now improves how accurately "
"they're transcribed"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Fixed a large blank gap that could appear in the transcript pane"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: downloading a model on first launch no longer fails with \"Could "
"not connect to the server\""
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Fixed: the recommended gemma4 models can now actually be downloaded "
"(updated built-in AI engine)"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Download problems now show a clear error message instead of silently "
"doing nothing"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "The app no longer leaves its AI engine running after you quit"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Simpler pre-call setup: meeting type is inferred, participants suggested "
"as chips"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "App version shown in the sidebar footer is now always accurate"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Downloads are now fully signed end-to-end"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "First release with automatic updates — the app now updates itself"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"New coaching signals from real-meeting testing: parked questions, vague "
"answers"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Turn-based signal engine with meeting types and adaptive thresholds"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid ""
"Dual-pipeline speaker detection: your mic vs. their audio — no more "
"guessing"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Benchmark harness: coaching quality is now scored against ground truth"
msgstr ""

#: CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Simpler interface: training panel removed, trends moved to Settings (⌘,)"
msgstr ""

